iption (shown by `pytest --markers`) still reads \"set HALLUCINOTE_SKIP_AUDIO=1 to skip in CPU-only/container sessions where that stack is unstable.\" A maintainer reading it keeps skipping audio in containers and loses that coverage for no reason. The change-log's \"that note is corrected\" is false for this site. Search for `unstable` / `HALLUCINOTE_SKIP_AUDIO` across pyproject.toml, .github/workflows/ci.yml and docs/. Make the marker text relational, e.g. \"opt-out: HALLUCINOTE_SKIP_AUDIO=1\", and drop the instability claim.", "files": ["pyproject.toml"], "fid": "R-4"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "note", "title": "`.testament.toml` setup comment says \"same sync as CI\", but it syncs with `--frozen` where CI uses `--locked`", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. CI runs `uv sync --all-packages --all-extras --locked`, which fails on a stale lock. The setup step's `--frozen` installs whatever uv.lock says without checking it, so on a stale lock a pool run goes green where CI goes red. Either switch the setup step to `--locked` so it really matches CI, or delete \"same sync as CI\".", "files": [".testament.toml"], "fid": "R-5"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "severity": "note", "title": "Per-process numba cache dirs leak when a process dies abnormally", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. `atexit` does not run on SIGSEGV or SIGKILL, or on an xdist worker that is torn down hard, so each such process leaves a `numba-cache-*` dir (a full librosa JIT cache) in the temp dir. Pool containers are ephemeral and macOS ages out $TMPDIR, so the cost is small. If it matters locally, sweep stale `numba-cache-*` dirs older than a day at conftest import.", "files": ["conftest.py"], "fid": "R-6"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "note", "title": "learnings cross-check: the numba-segfault learning now names a superseded remedy for pytest runs", "recommendation": "Scope: none. In core.md, \"A segfaulting suite reports a SMALLER suite\" say